Project: Royal Shine, a jewellery catalogue website with a Filament admin panel, built on Laravel.

HOSTING CONSTRAINT: The final hosting is not confirmed. It will probably be Hostinger shared hosting managed through cPanel/hPanel, with limited SSH access and no root access. Write all code to be shared-hosting-safe:

1. Do NOT depend on Redis, Docker, Supervisor, queue workers, Node.js on the server, Horizon, Octane, or any long-running process.
2. Set defaults in .env.example: CACHE_STORE=file, SESSION_DRIVER=file (or database), QUEUE_CONNECTION=sync, MAIL via SMTP.
3. All frontend assets (Tailwind, Alpine, Vite) are built locally. The built files in public/build must be deployable without running npm on the server.
4. Use GD for image processing, not Imagick.
5. File uploads must use a configurable filesystem disk (FILESYSTEM_DISK in .env). Do not hardcode paths. The app must still work if "php artisan storage:link" is not possible on the host.
6. Never use exec(), shell_exec(), or symlink() inside application code.
7. The app must work whether the web root points to /public or when public files are served from public_html with the Laravel core outside it. Use asset() and url() helpers only, never hardcoded absolute paths.
8. Keep dependencies minimal. Before adding any Composer package, tell me why it is needed and whether it works on shared hosting.
9. Keep memory and execution time use low: paginate everything, avoid loading large collections, process image uploads efficiently.
10. Do not write any deployment scripts or CI/CD yet. Deployment will be handled later.

Acknowledge these rules and confirm you will follow them in every future task.